/*
  =============================================================================
  === MSS LOG INPUT (SAP ORDER FORM) ===
  Layout follows the original MSS log app: tab bar (Add Log Entries, Log Table,
  Dashboard, Calendar, Fix Missing IDs), recent-entries sidebar, one card per
  entry row, a log table with batch edit/delete, and a dashboard. Colors are the
  company blue, yellow and red; the logo sits top right (set LOGO_URL to use the
  official art).

  LOADING RULES (thousands of equipment records)
  Nothing is bulk loaded. Every query is filtered and has a small row limit, and
  each tab only loads when it is opened:
    - SAP orders and equipment are searched on the server as the admin types
      (debounced, results cached per search so repeat searches are instant).
    - Selecting an order loads only that order's rows, then only the equipment
      those rows point at or are named after.
    - Log Table, Dashboard and Calendar load one filtered, limited page each.
    - Fix Missing IDs scans the log page by page and looks up candidate
      equipment per group of entries, never the whole equipment table.
  Text searches ask for the usual casings (as typed, lower, UPPER, Title), so
  they find matches even where the data source compares text case-sensitively.

  ADD LOG ENTRIES
  An admin types a SAP order (not case sensitive). Matching orders are suggested
  as they type; selecting one fills in its equipment from craa5_aa_ms_assets (one
  row per equipment, one column per frequency). Each line gets its equipment:
    1. the SAP row's craa5_asset lookup, when it is set ("linked");
    2. otherwise the best fit, picked automatically: equipment that earlier log
       entries of this order were saved to, then the same or a similar name in
       the same room AND area (equipment numbers must agree). The confidence
       is shown on the line.
  "Change" moves a line to the next best fit and lists the other candidates, a
  search of all equipment, and "Create new asset". When a line is changed, the
  earlier entries of this order that were saved to the wrong equipment (or with
  no equipment ID) are found and moved to the chosen equipment on submit.
  Missing equipment can also be added to the order. One craa5__log_ row is
  written per equipment:
    craa5_equipmentguid     = craa5_aa_assetsid (what mss - calendar matches on)
    craa5_equipment/room/area = display copies taken from the asset
    craa5_sap               = SAP order entered (upper case)
    craa5_lastcleaned       = completion date, midnight UTC
    craa5_lastcleanedby     = initials, upper case, "/" separated
    craa5_hoursworked       = number (the order's hours split across equipment)

  FIX MISSING IDS
  Repair IDs: scans the log page by page for entries whose craa5_equipmentguid
  is empty, points at equipment that no longer exists, or points at equipment
  in a different room/area than the entry names. Identical entries are grouped,
  the closest equipment is ranked (SAP order first, then name in the same room
  and area) and the chosen ID is written back.
  Unify duplicates: for one room (and optionally one area), finds equipment
  records that are the same equipment (same name; with the option ticked, also
  similar names) in the same room and area, and moves every log entry onto the
  one record that is kept.
  Nothing is saved until the admin applies.
  =============================================================================
*/

